# API Routes

Handlers live under `packages/app/src/app/api/` as method exports (`GET`, `POST`, `PATCH`, `DELETE`). `dispatchApi` in `packages/app/src/lib/dispatch-api.ts` matches the pathname and method. `/api/auth` goes to Better Auth; `/api/infra-metadata` is handled in `dispatchApi`.

Define handlers with `createRoute` from `@/lib/api-utils`. Validate params, query, and body with Zod schemas from `@/lib/route-schemas` or `@solstatus/common/db`.

```typescript
import { createRoute } from "@/lib/api-utils"
import { getWorkerEnv } from "@/lib/worker-env"
import { StatusCodes } from "http-status-codes"

export const GET = createRoute
  .params(idStringParamsSchema) // optional
  .query(paginationQuerySchema()) // optional
  .body(endpointMonitorsInsertDTOSchema) // optional
  .handler(async (request, context) => {
    const { env } = getWorkerEnv()
    const db = useDrizzle(env.DB)
    return Response.json(data, { status: StatusCodes.OK })
  })
```

Use `StatusCodes` and `ReasonPhrases` from `http-status-codes`. Access Cloudflare bindings with `getWorkerEnv()`. Use Drizzle via `useDrizzle(env.DB)`.
